window.AG_PRACTICE["junchen"] = {"id":"junchen","axis":"herb","seal":"草","scene":"art/scene-garden.jpg","title":"Formula Architecture","titleZh":"君臣佐使","sub":"How a formula is built, and how two herbs change each other","subZh":"方之結構，與藥之七情","mentor":{"key":"yao","nm":"Yào Wēng","nmZh":"藥翁","line":"\"A formula is not a pile of good herbs. It is a household: someone leads, someone assists, someone restrains the leader's temper, and someone shows the whole party to the right door.\"","lineZh":"「方不是一堆好藥堆在一起。方是一個家：有人主事，有人幫襯，有人管住主事的脾氣，還有人領路到門口。」"},"card":{"h":"The Household 君臣佐使","hZh":"","p":"Sovereign 君 addresses the main pattern. Minister 臣 strengthens the sovereign or handles a second complaint. Assistant 佐 helps, restrains the sovereign's harshness, or in stubborn cases opposes it deliberately. Envoy 使 guides the formula to the right channel and harmonises the whole.","pZh":"君藥治其主證；臣藥助君，或治其兼證；佐藥有佐助、佐制、反佐三義；使藥引經、調和諸藥。"},"note":"This deck is about formula structure as it is taught, not about prescribing. Herbal formulas are individualised and can interact with medication — they belong with a qualified practitioner. 本組所習者組方之理，非為處方。方藥須辨體而施，且可與西藥相互作用，當由合格醫者處理。","items":[{"k":"match","q":"Match each role to its job in a formula.","qZh":"配伍四職，各司其事。","pairs":[{"l":"Sovereign 君","lZh":"","r":"Treats the main pattern directly","rZh":"針對主病主證，起主要作用"},{"l":"Minister 臣","lZh":"","r":"Strengthens the sovereign, or treats a secondary complaint","rZh":"助君加強，或治兼病兼證"},{"l":"Assistant 佐","lZh":"","r":"Assists, restrains harshness, or opposes deliberately","rZh":"佐助、佐制、反佐"},{"l":"Envoy 使","lZh":"","r":"Guides to the channel and harmonises the whole","rZh":"引經報使、調和諸藥"}],"note":"Not every formula has all four, and a single herb can hold two roles. The structure is a way of reading a formula, not a quota to fill. 四職未必俱備，一藥亦可兼職。此為讀方之法，非填格之令。"},{"k":"mc","q":"In Si Jun Zi Tang 四君子湯, which herb is the sovereign?","qZh":"四君子湯，何為君藥？","opts":[{"t":"Ren Shen 人參 — it tonifies qi directly and powerfully","c":"人參 — 大補元氣，直當主證","ok":1,"note":"The pattern is Spleen and Stomach qi deficiency, so the sovereign is the strongest qi tonic. Bai Zhu 白朮 is minister — it strengthens the Spleen and dries damp. Fu Ling 茯苓 is assistant — it drains damp and helps Bai Zhu. Zhi Gan Cao 炙甘草 is envoy — it harmonises and adds a gentle tonifying effect. Four herbs, four roles, perfectly clean. 證為脾胃氣虛，故以大補元氣者為君。白朮為臣，健脾燥濕；茯苓為佐，滲濕助朮；炙甘草為使，調和兼補。四藥四職，最為明白。"},{"t":"Fu Ling 茯苓","c":"茯苓","ok":0,"note":"Fu Ling drains damp — a supporting action here, not the main one. 茯苓滲濕，於本方為佐而非君。"},{"t":"Zhi Gan Cao 炙甘草","c":"炙甘草","ok":0,"note":"Gan Cao harmonises and guides. It is the envoy in this formula. 甘草調和引和，於本方為使。"},{"t":"Bai Zhu 白朮","c":"白朮","ok":0,"note":"Bai Zhu is minister — it reinforces the sovereign's action on the Spleen. 白朮為臣，助君以健脾。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"What is a 佐制 assistant doing?","qZh":"佐制之藥，其用為何？","opts":[{"t":"Restraining the harshness or toxicity of the sovereign","c":"制君藥之峻烈或毒性","ok":1,"note":"When a sovereign is powerful but rough, an assistant softens the edge so the formula can still be taken — for example a warm sovereign paired with something that protects the fluids. The other two kinds are 佐助 (helping the main action) and 反佐 (a small opposing herb used when a stubborn pattern would otherwise reject the treatment). 君藥雖效而性峻者，佐以緩之，使方可服。其餘二義：佐助者助其主效，反佐者於格拒之證少用性反之藥。"},{"t":"Increasing the sovereign's dose","c":"增君藥之量","ok":0,"note":"Dose is a separate decision from role. 用量與配伍之職為二事。"},{"t":"Replacing the sovereign if it is unavailable","c":"君藥不備而代之","ok":0,"note":"Substitution changes the formula; it is not what an assistant does. 代之則方已異，非佐之義。"},{"t":"Guiding the formula to a channel","c":"引經報使","ok":0,"note":"That is the envoy 使. 此使藥之職。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each of the seven relations 七情 to what it means.","qZh":"七情配其義。","pairs":[{"l":"Xiang Xu 相須","lZh":"","r":"Two similar herbs strengthen each other","rZh":"性效相類，同用增效"},{"l":"Xiang Shi 相使","lZh":"","r":"One herb is the main, the other raises its effect","rZh":"一主一輔，輔者助其效"},{"l":"Xiang Wei 相畏","lZh":"","r":"One herb's harshness is reduced by another","rZh":"一藥之毒烈為他藥所制"},{"l":"Xiang Wu 相惡","lZh":"","r":"One herb weakens the other's effect","rZh":"一藥減他藥之效"},{"l":"Xiang Fan 相反","lZh":"","r":"Combined, they produce harm","rZh":"合用而生害"}],"note":"The seventh is Dan Xing 單行, a single herb used alone. Xiang Sha 相殺 is the mirror of Xiang Wei: the herb that does the restraining. Note that Xiang Wu and Xiang Fan are the two to avoid — and the classical Eighteen Incompatibles 十八反 and Nineteen Antagonisms 十九畏 list the traditional cautions. 其七為單行。相殺者，制毒之一方，與相畏相對而言。相惡、相反二者當避；古有十八反、十九畏之戒。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which four qi 四氣 are used to describe an herb's temperature?","qZh":"四氣為何？","opts":[{"t":"Cold, cool, warm, hot","c":"寒、涼、溫、熱","ok":1,"note":"Plus neutral 平 for herbs that lean neither way. The principle behind it is simple and absolute: a cold pattern is treated with warm herbs, a hot pattern with cool ones — 寒者熱之，熱者寒之. 另有性平者不偏寒熱。其則至簡而不可違：寒者熱之，熱者寒之。"},{"t":"Acrid, sweet, bitter, salty","c":"辛、甘、苦、鹹","ok":0,"note":"Those are flavours 五味 (with sour 酸 making five), and they describe direction of action rather than temperature. 此五味之四（尚有酸），言其趨向而非寒熱。"},{"t":"Ascending, descending, floating, sinking","c":"升、降、浮、沉","ok":0,"note":"That is the fourth property — where in the body an herb tends to act. 此升降浮沉，言其作用之部位趨向。"},{"t":"Spring, summer, autumn, winter","c":"春、夏、秋、冬","ok":0,"note":"Seasons, not herb properties. 此時令，非藥性。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"An herb is described as acrid and warm, entering the Lung channel. What is it likely to do?","qZh":"某藥辛溫，歸肺經，其用當如何？","opts":[{"t":"Disperse and release the exterior, opening the Lung","c":"發散解表，宣通肺氣","ok":1,"note":"Acrid disperses, warm counters cold, and the channel says where. Fresh ginger — the reward from chapter one — is exactly this description. Reading the three properties together is how you predict an herb's use before you have memorised it. 辛主散，溫以勝寒，歸經指其所至。生薑即此三性之合，亦本遊戲第一章所得之藥。三性合讀，則藥未熟記而其用可推。"},{"t":"Nourish yin and moisten dryness","c":"滋陰潤燥","ok":0,"note":"That would be sweet and cool or cold, usually entering Lung and Stomach. 彼當甘而涼寒，多歸肺胃。"},{"t":"Drain fire and dry damp","c":"瀉火燥濕","ok":0,"note":"That would be bitter and cold. 彼當苦而寒。"},{"t":"Astringe and stop leakage","c":"收斂固澀","ok":0,"note":"That would be sour or astringent. 彼當酸或澀。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Why does the same pattern sometimes get different formulas in two different patients?","qZh":"同證而異方，何以然？","opts":[{"t":"Because the constitution, the season, the age and any second pattern all modify the prescription","c":"因其人之體質、時令、年歲、兼證而增損","ok":1,"note":"This is 辨證論治 — treatment determined by pattern, and the pattern is always the pattern *of this person*. A base formula is modified: herbs added for a second complaint, doses adjusted, harsh herbs softened for a frail patient. Same name, different formula. 此辨證論治：證者，此人此時之證也。故以成方為基而加減：兼證則增藥，虛弱則減其峻，各隨其人。"},{"t":"Because practitioners disagree about basic theory","c":"因醫者於基本理論不合","ok":0,"note":"Variation is mostly individualisation, not disagreement. 其異多為因人制宜，非理之爭。"},{"t":"Because formulas are chosen by preference","c":"因隨醫者所好而選","ok":0,"note":"Formulas are chosen by pattern, then modified for the person. 方從證出，而後因人加減。"},{"t":"Because the herbs available differ","c":"因藥材有無不同","ok":0,"note":"Availability can force substitution, but it is not the main reason. 藥材有無誠可致代用，然非主因。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which caution belongs in every discussion of herbal formulas?","qZh":"論方藥時，何項提醒必不可少？","opts":[{"t":"Herbs can interact with medication and are not self-prescribed","c":"藥可與西藥相互作用，不宜自行服用","ok":1,"note":"Interactions with anticoagulants, thyroid medication, sedatives and others are real and documented. Pregnancy has its own list of contraindicated herbs. Herbal treatment belongs with a qualified practitioner who knows the patient's full medication list — and this game teaches the reasoning, not the prescribing. 與抗凝、甲狀腺、鎮靜等藥之相互作用確有其實。妊娠另有禁忌之品。用藥當由合格醫者，並須知其全部用藥。本遊戲所授者理，非處方。"},{"t":"Herbs are natural and therefore always safe","c":"藥出天然，故必無害","ok":0,"note":"Not true, and the classical literature says so itself: the Eighteen Incompatibles and the pregnancy contraindications exist precisely because herbs are powerful. 非也。古籍自有十八反、妊娠禁忌，正因藥力非輕。"},{"t":"Doses do not matter in TCM","c":"中藥不論劑量","ok":0,"note":"Dose changes the role an herb plays in a formula and can change its safety. 量之增減，既變其職，亦關其安。"},{"t":"Formulas never need modification","c":"成方不必加減","ok":0,"note":"Modification for the individual is the norm. 隨證加減，乃常法。"}]},{"k":"order","q":"Put these four steps of prescribing in their classical order.","qZh":"排出論治四步之序。","seq":[{"t":"Differentiate the pattern","c":"辨證"},{"t":"Establish the treatment principle","c":"立法"},{"t":"Choose the formula","c":"選方"},{"t":"Adjust the herbs and doses","c":"用藥（加減）"}],"note":"辨證 → 立法 → 選方 → 用藥. Skipping straight from a symptom to a formula is the commonest mistake — and it is the same mistake as skipping from a cough to a point. 由證而法，由法而方，由方而藥。見症即方，最為常誤——與見咳即取一穴，其失一也。"},{"k":"mc","q":"An envoy herb 使藥 is often included even when the formula already works. Why?","qZh":"方已可用而仍加使藥，何也？","opts":[{"t":"To direct the formula to the right channel and to harmonise the other herbs","c":"引經報使，並調和諸藥","ok":1,"note":"Two jobs. A guiding herb takes the formula where the pattern is — the same herbs sent to a different channel treat a different complaint. And a harmonising herb such as Gan Cao smooths the interaction between herbs that would otherwise clash or gripe the stomach. 二職：引經者，使藥力達於病所，同藥異引則所治亦異；調和者，如甘草，使諸藥不相牴牾，亦護胃氣。"},{"t":"To make the formula taste better","c":"為改其味","ok":0,"note":"Palatability is a real consideration but it is not what the envoy category means. 適口誠亦一慮，然非使藥之義。"},{"t":"To reach the classical count of four roles","c":"以足四職之數","ok":0,"note":"The four roles are a description, not a quota. 四職為說理之分，非填數之令。"},{"t":"To increase the total dose","c":"以增總量","ok":0,"note":"Total dose is set by the pattern and the patient. 總量從證從人。"}]}]};
